      "side": 1,
      "message": "As maze@ points out, null is likely better here. EMPTY_UPSTREAM seems reasonable at first glance, but the truth is that a) we don\u0027t actually have an upstream, and having a non-null UpstreamInfo is confusing, and b) EMPTY_UPSTREAM behaves very differently from an actual upstream, so any methods actually using UpstreamInfo objects will have to be very careful about what they do.\n\nIt seems better to return null instead of returning EMPTY_UPSTREAM, and do a null check in line 948:\n\n\n        final UpstreamInfo currUpstreamInfo \u003d getUpstreamInfoV4(ns);\n\n        // TODO: replace mLastIPv4UpstreamIfindex by mIpv4UpstreamInfo.\n        final int upstreamIndex \u003d (currUpstreamInfo !\u003d null) ? currUpstreamInfo.ifIndex : 0;\n        if (mLastIPv4UpstreamIfindex \u003d\u003d upstreamIndex) return;",
